line	<str>With the Spy captured, we attempted to interrogate him using some Truth Serum. However, the Spy was able to destroy it.</str>
line	<str>To make some more Truth Serum, I prepared an Enriched Snapdragon Seed and planted it in a Specially Prepared Patch on the roof of the White Knights' Castle. While waiting for it to grow, I recruited Turael, Mazchna, Duradel and Cyrisus to our cause.</str>
line	<str>I harvested the Enriched Snapdragon and used it to make some new Truth Serum. I then administered the Truth Serum to the Spy and he provided details on an individual known as the Dark Squall.</str>
line	<str>Based on the information provided, Idria and Akrisae initiated a search for the Dark Squall. I then recruited Harrallak Menarous, Ghommal and Sloane to our cause. However, while discussing our next steps, Hazelmere arrived and volunteered to join us as well.</str>
line	<str>I spoke to Akrisae and he told me there had been a possible sighting of the Dark Squall at the Black Knights' Fortress. He sent Silif to investigate, but lost contact with him. I travelled to the Black Knights' Fortress myself to investigate. I found Silif imprisoned in some Catacombs beneath the Fortress.</str>
line	<str>I managed to free Silif from his imprisonment in the Black Knight Catacombs and gave him a Disguise. While he gathered Intelligence, I set out to find the Dark Squall. However, upon finding him, I discovered him to actually be Surok Magis. He recognised me and attacked, but I was able to defeat him and plant a Teleorb on him.</str>
line	<str>I returned to the White Knights' Castle and updated the others on what happened in the Black Knight Catacombs. Using information found by Silif, we were able to locate Lucien's Camp near the Wilderness.</str>
line	<str>I travelled to Lucien's Camp and confronted Lucien with the Heroes. However, he was too powerful for us. Duradel, Turael, Sloane, Cyrisus, Ghommal and Hazelmere were all killed. The rest of us were forced to flee.</str>
line	<str>Despite the situation looking dire, Akrisae presented a potential new lead. According to him, Movario was spotted entering a cavern full of Floating Lights in the Lumbridge Swamp Caves.</str>
line	<str>I found Movario in the Lumbridge Swamp Caves. By disguising myself as the Dark Squall, I managed to convince him that I was there to help him find the Stone of Jas.</str>
line	<str>Using information provided by Movario, I was able to reach the bottom of a Large Chasm by attracting a Light Creature with a Sapphire Lantern. I searched the area and managed to open a tunnel into an Ancient Temple.</str>
line	<str>I explored the Ancient Temple and found the Stone of Jas. However, upon finding it, I was attacked by some sort of Elemental Creature which I was forced to defeat. I then touched the Stone and was granted a Strange Vision. However, Movario arrived at the same time, shortly followed by Lucien.</str>
line	<col=000080><col=800000>Lucien</col> teleported away with the <col=800000>Stone</col> and summoned some <col=800000>Demons</col>, but I was able to defeat them with ease thanks to powers granted to me by the <col=800000>Stone of Jas</col>. I should return to the <col=800000>White Knights' Castle</col> and let the others know what happened.</col>
step	24	-	Pre-release
line	<col=000080>This quest is coming soon...</col>
line	<col=000080>When it releases, I can start it by talking to <col=800000>Ivy Sophista</col> in <col=800000>Taverley</col>.</col>
